{"schema_version":1,"snapshot":"2021-12-03","source":{"repository":"matthiaskoenig/pkdb_analysis","path":"tests/data/testdata_concise_false.zip","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matthiaskoenig/pkdb_analysis/develop/tests/data/testdata_concise_false.zip"},"sid":"2584298","namespace":"pmid","name":"Chen1989","licence":"closed","access":"public","date":"2021-07-13","creator":"janekg","curators":["janekg"],"substances":["codeine","codeine phosphate","codeine-6-glucuronide"],"identifiers":{"source_study_sid":"2584298","pmid":"2584298","pmcid":null,"doi":null,"pkdb_sid":null},"reference":{"title":"Direct determination of codeine-6-glucuronide in plasma and urine using solid-phase extraction and high-performance liquid chromatography with fluorescence detection.","date":"1989-12-26","journal":"Journal of chromatography","authors":["Z R Chen","G Reynolds","F Bochner","A Somogyi"],"abstract":"A sensitive and selective method was developed for the direct determination of codeine-6-glucuronide in plasma and urine using high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) with fluorescence detection. Codeine-6-glucuronide was synthesised and its purity estimated using acid and enzyme hydrolysis. The hydrolysis of codeine-6-glucuronide by beta-glucuronidase was incomplete and urine reduced the extent of hydrolysis. Codeine-6-glucuronide was recovered from plasma using a solid-phase extraction column and separated on a reversed-phase C18 HPLC column. The assay showed good reproducibility and accuracy (within 10%), and standard curves were linear between 32 and 1600 ng/ml in plasma and between 0.32 and 160 micrograms/ml in urine. The assay has been applied to the study of the pharmacokinetics and metabolism of codeine in patients."},"row_counts":{"groups":3,"individuals":5,"interventions":1,"outputs":26,"timecourses":2,"scatters":0},"entity_counts":{"groups":1,"individuals":1,"interventions":1,"outputs":26,"timecourses":2,"scatters":0},"groups":[{"study_name":"Chen1989","measurem